# Intro
A `c_hyp` sweep of the LW/FUV hyperbolic (Cattaneo/P1-relaxation) propagation
scheme, from `c_hyp ~ c` down to `c_hyp << c`, at both a star-sourced field
and a star-free seeded Gaussian pulse (`FUVSpecificEnergy`/`LWSpecificEnergy`
in the IC). Measures the scheme's `c_hyp`-independent steady state and
`c_hyp`-dependent transient (self-similarity and retardation), and locates
the triggered-dissipation term's own Courant/stability bound empirically.

## Why the propagation speed cannot be swept with LW_FUV_c_hyp_margin alone
The closure `c_hyp = C_hyp*h/dt` ties the propagation speed to the local
resolution and time-step so that the hyperbolic CFL condition holds as an
equality, not an inequality that could be violated. `C_hyp`
(`GEARFeedback:LW_FUV_c_hyp_margin`) has a legal range of `(0, 1.7]`, which
at this example's resolution spans `c_hyp` from about 0.98 to 33 km/s: a
factor of 34, nowhere near either end of the physically interesting range.
Reaching `c_hyp -> c` or `c_hyp << c` needs
`LW_FUV_c_hyp_pin_for_debugging`, which overwrites `c_hyp` after the closure
and after the light-speed clamp, making the effective Courant number
`nu_eff = c_hyp*dt/h` a free quantity that this example's check script
measures and reports rather than assumes. **This parameter must never be
used in a production run.** `LW_FUV_dissipation_alpha_pin_for_debugging`
plays the analogous role for the dissipation trigger: it fixes the
coefficient a smooth pulse's trigger might otherwise leave at zero, so Leg N
tests the coefficient the stability bound is actually stated in terms of.

## Metallicity
The FUV/LW screening length scales with metallicity; at solar `Z` a seeded
pulse is absorbed within a handful of steps, leaving nothing to measure.
`initial_metallicity` defaults to 0.05 here (Legs P, N) so absorption stays
negligible over the run; Legs R and I use their own values (see `run.sh`).

## Cooling
`GrackleCooling:disable_cooling_for_debugging: 1` keeps the gas's thermal and
dynamical state fixed (`chemistry_data` still resolves, since `--cooling` is
passed), isolating the propagated field from gas response. Leg P's slowest
runs still drift the gas somewhat via other channels; the check script
reports this drift and voids the affected gates rather than silently
ignoring it.

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_0 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j
```

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Override any parameter via the matching env var: gas density (`gas_density`,
atom/cm^3), gas particle mass (`gas_mass`, Msun), resolution level (`level`),
`seed_pulse` (>0: star-free seeded pulse; 0: star source), `c_hyp_pin`
(`LW_FUV_c_hyp_pin_for_debugging`, km/s), `c_hyp_margin`
(`LW_FUV_c_hyp_margin`), `alpha_max`/`alpha_pin`
(`LW_FUV_dissipation_alpha_max`/`..._pin_for_debugging`), `propagation`
(`LW_FUV_propagation`), `initial_metallicity`, `time_end`, `dt_max`,
`dt_min`, `delta_time`, and thread count (`n_threads`); see `run.sh` for the
full list and defaults. `run_name=<dir> ./run.sh` moves the run's outputs
into `<dir>` once done, to keep more than one run's outputs side by side.
The full run table (Legs P, N, R, I) and their env-var settings are recorded
separately in this project's own validation records, not in this file.

# Checking
```
python3 isrf_propagation_speed_sweep_check.py --c-hyp-pin $c_hyp_pin --c-hyp-margin $c_hyp_margin
python3 sweep_compare.py --mode {P,N,RI} --runs dir1 dir2 ...
```
`run.sh` runs the per-run check automatically. It measures the run's own
`nu_eff` and the dissipation-term stability bound at the run's own alpha,
the pulse front position, a gas-drift control, and (for N-type runs invoked
with `--expect-unstable`) whether the run destabilized as predicted.

`sweep_compare.py` performs the cross-run comparisons: self-similarity and
retardation collapse across a fixed-Courant sweep (gated, `--mode P`), the
stability bound's bracketing location across a Courant-number sweep (gated,
`--mode N`), and reachability reporting for the star-sourced and
propagation-on/off legs (report only, `--mode RI`). A dt-quantization
mismatch across a `--mode P` sweep is detected and reported as the run set
being INVALID rather than a physics failure; re-run with `time_end` adjusted
if this happens.
